  "note": "Triennial election of the 23 electoral divisions of Limavady rural district, one member each, polled on 5 June 1952. Twenty-seven candidates were nominated and four divisions were contested; the Nationalists gained two seats and with them control of the council. Two Nationalists contesting a seat already held by the Nationalists; M'Laughlin was the outgoing member."
